   - Components in src/components/ui/ come from shadcn-vue (MIT) and reka-ui (MIT).

5. Files copied from the owner's old site (provenance: "from the owner's old site")
   - Partner logos in public/partners/ (webp, resized): detexi, dinkes, kawalcorona (Ethical Hacker Indonesia),
     inacovid, sultenglawancovid, banuacoders from the pico-api-docs repository (MIT, banua-coder/pico-api-docs,
     public/*.webp); kawalcovid, pikobar, vuejs from the owner's old Hostinger storage (storage/images/partner).
     The logos are trademarks of their owners and are shown only to name the partners and data sources.
   - Banner and donation pictures in public/media/{banners,donations}/ (webp, resized) from the owner's old
     Hostinger storage (storage/banners, storage/donations). They were uploaded by the owner and by the donation
     organisers for the old site. Not MIT. Every picture was looked at before it was kept (personal data review):
       - the 4 banners show organisation names and logos and illustrations only: kept;
       - of the 8 donation posters, 7 were removed because they show phone numbers, bank account numbers or
         names of private persons (or a person's face): Naga/PSMTI posko, "Informasi" (Seh'at), Posko Jaga Palu,
         SIGI Mosijagai, Isoman Care, bakubantu, Join the fight. Kept: "Kongsi Gambar Serrupa" (an illustration,
         no personal data). The donation cards that had a removed poster show the title only.
     The Isoman page still shows the bank account numbers the API gives for each donation, as text (the owner's
     decision, not changed here); those are the donors' public appeals from 2021.
   - Map boundary files (item 1) were also found in the old Hostinger storage (storage/geojson), same status.

6. Libraries of the old site that are not used
   The old site drew its maps with AnyChart 8 (commercial licence, watermark in the free build) and its charts
   with Chart.js 3 and chartjs-plugin-zoom. None of their code is in this repository. The maps and charts are
   rebuilt on d3-geo (build time) and d3-scale/d3-shape (client), both ISC licence. Unovis was evaluated and not
   adopted (docs/adr/0001-chart-library.md).

7. Brand v2 illustrations (written for PICO, MIT)
   public/illustrations/{light,dark}/: cuci-tangan, pakai-masker, jaga-jarak, vaksinasi, gejala-demam, gejala-batuk,
   gejala-sakit-kepala, gejala-sesak-napas, gejala-hilang-penciuman, isolasi-mandiri, telekonsultasi, bantuan-antar, rumah-sakit,
   state-kosong, state-galat, state-luring, state-memuat, state-periode-kosong, state-pemeliharaan, telepon-119. Source: the PICO brand
   repository, brand/v2/flat (scripts/copy-illustrations.sh copies them). Used on the home page, Wiki, Kontak and Isoman, and in the
   empty, error, offline, loading and no-data-for-period states (page size 200 px, in a card or chart 96 px).
   Lottie: public/lottie/{loading,success,offline,empty,handwash-loop,logo-reveal,logo-reveal-dark}.json and posters/*.svg from the same
   source (written for PICO, MIT). Player: lottie-web (MIT, Copyright Airbnb), light SVG build, loaded as its own chunk only when a moment
   is in view and motion is not reduced. No Lottie file comes from LottieFiles or another third party.
